.TH IO_WAITWRITE 3
.SH NAME
io_waitwrite \- write data to a file descriptor, waiting if necessary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <io.h>
.PP
.BI "int64 io_waitwrite(fd_type " d ", const char* " buf ", int64 " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B io_waitwrite
writes up to
.I len
bytes of data from the buffer
.I buf
to the file descriptor
.IR d .
.PP
If the file descriptor
.I d
is marked as non-blocking within the library's I/O context, the function will block until the file descriptor is ready for writing (using
.BR poll (2)
on POSIX or socket manipulation on Windows) before attempting the write operation.
.PP
On POSIX systems, the function also invokes
.BR io_sigpipe (3)
to ensure proper handling of SIGPIPE signals.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.TP
.B >= 0
The number of bytes successfully written.
.TP
.B -3
An error occurred;
.I errno
is set to indicate the cause (e.g., EBADF, EPIPE).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR io_waitread (3),
.BR poll (2),
.BR write (2)